1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,600
Hello and welcome
to Real Easy English,

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:08,040
the podcast where we have
real conversations in easy English

3
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:09,440
to help you learn.

4
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,200
I'm Beth.

5
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:11,320
And I'm Neil.

6
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:15,360
There is a video version
of this podcast on our website,

7
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:19,920
where you can also find a worksheet
and transcript to help you learn.

8
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:22,840
It's at bbclearningenglish.com.

9
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,120
Hi, Neil.
How are you?

10
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,080
I'm hungry.

11
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:35,560
Me too. I'm starving.

12
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:40,400
Well, that's good, because
we're talking about lunch today.

13
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:45,200
We're recording this just
before lunch, so it's no wonder that

14
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:46,480
we're both very hungry.

15
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:52,480
You might be able to hear our
tummies rumble because we're hungry.

16
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:54,560
OK. So, shall we begin?

17
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:55,760
Yes. Let's do it.

18
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,120
What have you got for lunch today?

19
00:00:58,120 --> 00:01:06,200
Today for my lunch, I have chicken
with potatoes and vegetables

20
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:08,600
in a harissa paste.

21
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:11,000
Oh, that sounds really nice.

22
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,040
Yeah, it's leftovers actually,

23
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:17,560
which I have heated up
and brought in, in a little flask.

24
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:19,440
What are leftovers?

25
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:20,960
Good question. Leftovers.

26
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:25,560
That's food from a meal that you've
already had that you didn't finish

27
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:28,560
and you can heat it up
and eat it again.

28
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:32,560
Yes. I also have leftovers
for my lunch today.

29
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:41,680
So, yesterday I made a pasta for lunch
with vegetables in it

30
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,400
and I have that.

31
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,560
So, Beth, what do you usually have
for lunch?

32
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:50,040
Is it usually leftovers
or something else?

33
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:56,360
It's usually leftovers when I come
into work because it's easier,

34
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:59,240
and then I don't need to buy lunch.

35
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:02,400
But if I go out and buy food,

36
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:08,880
then I would usually go for something
like sushi or ramen.

37
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:13,800
What about you?
What do you usually have for lunch?

38
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,960
Yeah. Sometimes I have leftovers
that I bring in.

39
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:20,480
Sometimes I buy a sandwich,
for example.

40
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:24,280
What's your favourite kind
of sandwich?

41
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,640
If I have a sandwich...

42
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:32,120
if I buy a sandwich for lunch, I like
to get things like smoked salmon.

43
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:34,560
Nice, with pickles maybe.

44
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:36,120
Yeah.

45
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:41,440
There's a really good baguette I like
actually that has smoked salmon

46
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:44,280
and egg mayonnaise in it.

47
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,520
Oh, it's so nice.

48
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:46,120
Stop it.

49
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:46,640
Sorry.

50
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:47,600
I'm so hungry.

51
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:51,280
Me too. Neil, do you ever skip lunch?

52
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:53,320
No. No way!

53
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:57,960
I would be in a horrible mood
if I skipped lunch.

54
00:02:57,960 --> 00:03:02,520
I don't understand
how anyone can skip any meal.

55
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:05,480
I need to eat all my meals.

56
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:07,920
Yeah. Otherwise, you get hangry.

57
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:11,960
Exactly. 'Hangry' is hungry and angry.

58
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:16,840
I'm on the...
I'm almost getting hangry now.

59
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,720
What's your favourite meal?
Is it lunch?

60
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:22,880
Breakfast? Dinner?

61
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:28,960
I think the evening meal is probably
my favourite because we sit at the table

62
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:33,240
and chat and it's the biggest,
nicest meal of the day

63
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:38,040
and you don't really have to do
anything after so you can relax.

64
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:39,600
Mmm. Yeah, that's good.

65
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:44,120
I really like brunch, which is
that sort of in between breakfast

66
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:46,640
and lunch – maybe 10:00.

67
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:52,400
And I might have eggs and bacon
and hash browns and avocado,

68
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:57,440
a big meal full of lots of good food.
I like a brunch.

69
00:03:57,440 --> 00:04:00,800
Do you ever have a working lunch?

70
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:06,720
I do occasionally
if I'm working from home.

71
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:10,920
because I can carry on working
and eat quickly.

72
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:15,280
And then in my actual lunch break,
I might have a nice long walk

73
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:17,000
or something like that,

74
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,360
but when I'm in the office,
I don't want to eat at my desk.

75
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:21,560
No. Me neither.

76
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:24,520
I don't really like working lunches.

77
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:29,080
I would rather eat my lunch
without working.

78
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:32,680
Yeah, I'd prefer the same, really.

79
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:41,720
Let's recap the language we heard
during the conversation.

80
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:45,920
We had 'skip',
which means not have or do.

81
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:49,600
For example, I never skip lunch.

82
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:55,520
We heard 'working lunch', which is when
you eat your lunch while you're working.

83
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:59,680
We also had 'leftovers',
which is when you don't finish a meal

84
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:03,800
so you have more of it at
a different time, like the next day.

85
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:07,320
And we talked about which meals
and food we 'prefer'.

86
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:11,360
If you prefer something, you like it
better than something else.

87
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:16,000
Yes. And another phrase we can use
to say this is 'would rather'.

88
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:20,800
For example, I'd rather have sushi
than a sandwich for lunch.

89
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:23,400
That's it for this episode
of Real Easy English.

90
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:26,120
Test what you've learned
with a worksheet on our website,

91
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,480
bbclearningenglish.com.

92
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:33,560
And make sure you join us again for
another easy English conversation.

93
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:34,960
We'll be back next week.

94
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:36,160
See you soon.

95
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:37,200
Goodbye!